---
description: Non-negotiable Salon product and domain invariants
alwaysApply: true
---

- Treat `docs/MARKETPLACE_REQUIREMENTS.md` as product direction and `docs/PRODUCT_SPEC.md` as the implementation source of truth; do not silently broaden scope.
- User-facing roles: **Talent** and **Buyer** (legacy persistence: `entertainer` / `venue`). **Agency** is coming-soon only — not selectable and not persisted until specified.
- Account status is `active` or `suspended`. Self-serve signup creates an active account with exactly one marketplace role (talent XOR buyer). Staff may suspend/reactivate; there is no staff account-approval wait to enter the marketplace.
- Model buyer locations as **one venue per buyer account** (`venues.owner_user_id` unique) with **one room** for calendar ownership. Team memberships / multi-venue orgs are out of scope until specified. One account holds one role type only (no dual-role). Future multi-talent agencies are supply-side orgs, not a third XOR signup role.
- Enforce role-segregated discovery on the server: talent discovers locations/opportunities only; buyers discover talent only; staff may moderate both.
- Unpublished profiles (`publication_state` ≠ `approved`) are invisible in discovery. Active members may search the opposite side before publishing, but may not contact (apply / send or respond to direct requests) until their own profile is published.
- Keep contact values hidden until shortlist or accepted direct request.
- Route applications and direct requests into one booking state machine.
- Confirm only after both parties sign the current agreement version; deposit status is independent.
- German agreement text controls; English is a labeled convenience translation.
- Confirmed bookings block both calendars. Holds expire. Never permit overlapping confirmed resource bookings.
- Do not add public directories/events/reviews, chat, payments/escrow, live legal claims, or automatic staff verification without a spec change. Owner self-publish with a built-in QA checklist is in scope.
- External calendar sync is a separate milestone; do not claim it operational until provisioned.
